  "facts": [
    "Three fixed 14-release trajectories retain all 14 placements and all 3 stars on final, matching the baseline completion outcome.",
    "On those trajectories, maximum horizontal displacement of the oldest seven bodies falls by about 6.7 to 7.7 percent. These are bounded single-run measurements, not player success probabilities.",
    "The fixed 28-release pressure policy ends in large_collapse after release15 on baseline and final. Final cumulativePlaced is13 versus14 baseline. Long-tower survivability has not improved in this test.",
    "In the easy fixed collision fixture final settles after contact at roughly0.739/0.725/0.630 seconds for depth0/300/600. The600-depth transient angle peak is higher; reduced residual motion does not promise uniformly smaller impact peaks.",
    "Both before and final already have zero tail angular velocity during the last second of this easy fixture. It does not establish large gameplay gains.",
    "Final has no horizontal impulse path; all18 reported structure/safety assertions passed and errors are empty. A completed diagnostic suite is not the same as demonstrated surprise."
